        & \qquad + \underbrace{ \alpha_{n}^2 {\mathbb E} \left[ \left( -B_1 {\check{x}}_{n} + \frac{R_{n}^x }{ \alpha_{n} } \right)^\top \nabla^2 f({\check{x}}_{n}) \left( -B_1 {\check{x}}_{n} + \frac{R_{n}^x }{ \alpha_{n} } \right) \Big| {\mathcal F}_{n} \right] }_{2 R^f_{n,4}}.
    \end{split} \label{eq:lem:generator-twotime:f3}
\end{align}
Recall that $\tilde{\xi}_{n} = \xi_{n} - \kappa_{n} H^\star \psi_{n}$ with $\kappa_{n} = \beta_{n} / \alpha_{n} = o(1)$. Then we have ${\mathbb E} [ \tilde{\xi}_{n} \tilde{\xi}_{n}^\top | {\mathcal F}_{n} ] \overset{p}{\to} \Sigma_\xi $.
Moreover, Assumption~\ref{assump:noise-fclt} ensures each entry of ${\mathbb E} [ \tilde{\xi}_{n} \tilde{\xi}_{n}^\top | {\mathcal F}_{n} ]$ is uniformly integrable, which together with convergence in probability imply ${\mathbb E} \| {\mathbb E} [ \tilde{\xi}_{n} \tilde{\xi}_{n}^\top | {\mathcal F}_{n} ] - \Sigma_{\xi}  \| \to 0 $.




From our assumptions and the results in Assumption~\ref{assump:mart-decouple-rate} and Lemma~\ref{lem:check-twotime-xy}, we have 
\begin{align}\label{eq:lem:generator-twotime:f4}
